; Output: TIE_SLUR.M
; Console: TIE_SLUR.OUT
; PMDMML.MAN §4-10

#Title TIE_SLUR
#Option /v/c

; §4-10 Tie/Slur Specification (& &&)
A c4&c4                 ; Tie (notes joined)
A d8&&d8                ; Slur (notes re-articulated smoothly)
A e4&8                  ; Tie with length addition (e4 + e8)
A f8&&4                 ; Slur with length specification (f8 then f4 slur)

; --- Part B: Tie/slur combinations ---
; Tie (single &)
B @1 c4&c4 d8&d8 e2&e4
; Slur (double &&)
B d8&&d8 e4&&e4
; Tie with length only (no second note)
B f4&8 g8&4
; Mixed tie and slur
B c4&c4&&c4 d

; Tie extends note
D @1 c4&8 d2&4 e8&16

; --- sular: tied note after slur ---
; The & (tie) followed by a note exercises the sular path
; which needs bp8 call for correct length compression
D @1 c4&c4 d8&d8 e2&e4 f16&f16

; --- Tie & without preceding note (tie_norm prsok&1==0) ---
A @1 c&d e

; --- Slur && with explicit length (sular path) ---
A c4&&4 d

; More tie patterns for tieset_2 coverage
; Tie with explicit length that doesn't overflow
A c4&8 d8&4
; Slur with explicit length
A e4&&8 f8&&4

; Tied rest (rest after note with &)
A c4&r4 d

; Note compression: same note repeated for press (prsok & 4 path)
A c4&4 c4

; More press paths: consecutive same notes with ties
A c8 c8 c8 c8

; Tie with explicit length causing overflow (needs len >= 256 total)
; c%200 = 200 ticks, &%100 tries to add 100 -> 300 > 256
A c%200&%100

; Tie with length addition that overflows 256 (c%200 + %200 = 400 > 256)
A c%200&%200

; Tie/repeat and gate envelope helpers
A c&c         ; basic tie
